obligation.partial_result:
The closed results establish two endpoints of the desired adaptation problem.  First, the projection region \(\mathcal C_n\) has finite-sample coverage at least \(1-\alpha\) for the entire sharp closure, including at \(\tau_{a,b}^r(P)=0\).  Second, along the explicit SDC family, every estimator satisfies the boundary lower bound
\[
 \liminf_{n\to\infty}\inf_{\widehat I_n}
 \max_{P\in\{P_0,P_{\varepsilon_n}\}}
 \mathbb E_{P^n}\rho_H\!\left(\widehat I_n,\mathcal I_{\partial,q}(P)\right)
 \ge\frac{3}{20}
 \quad\text{whenever}\quad \varepsilon_n>0,\ \varepsilon_n=o(n^{-1}).
\]
Thus uniform shrinking is impossible at zero slack, while honest nonshrinking projection is available.  The frozen primitives do not yet determine an intermediate optimal rate solely as a function of \(\kappa_n\).
